    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean yeah the sherman act is old but it's still used for a reason. honestly though, i'm hearing a lot of people say that these investigations are basically just a way for the government to kill innovation because they don't understand how these platforms actually work. do you think there's a real risk that these lawsuits will actually end up hurting consumers in the long run by breaking up stuff that works well? or is that just a talking point from the tech companies?",
